# Frontend .env.example
# Copy this file to `frontend/.env` for local development and fill with real values.
# DO NOT commit real `.env` files containing credentials.
# Vite exposes env vars to the browser only when they are prefixed with `VITE_`.
# Supabase client-side values are public (anon) keys — safe for the frontend but still
# treat them carefully and rotate if accidentally exposed.

# Your Supabase project URL (found in Supabase dashboard → Settings → API)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Your Supabase anon/public key (found in Supabase dashboard → Settings → API)
# This key is intended for client-side usage. Do NOT place service_role keys here.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Notes:
# - Keep `.env` out of version control. Use this file as a template only.
# - For production, use your hosting platform's secret store or environment settings.
# - If keys are exposed, rotate them immediately. See SECURITY_ENV_SETUP.md for guidance.
